::SPEECH_U05_L07_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L07_GuidedPractice_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.DIG.01
Question:
Which choice best prepares an online speech product for publication?
{
~A. Publish the first draft without reviewing it#This choice is incomplete because it does not support clear publication, revision, audience awareness, or digital presentation quality.
=B. Revise content, check slide design, confirm notes match slides, and submit the final version#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
~C. Ignore audience needs during final review#This choice reflects a misconception. Recheck revision, publication readiness, audience impact, or slide coherence.
~D. Let everyone edit without roles or version control#This choice weakens the communication product because it ignores how the audience will use or understand it.
}
::SPEECH_U05_L07_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L07_GuidedPractice_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.03
Question:
Which role best supports collaborative publication?
{
~A. Publish the first draft without reviewing it#This choice is incomplete because it does not support clear publication, revision, audience awareness, or digital presentation quality.
~B. Add more decoration instead of improving meaning#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully meet the communication purpose or collaboration standard.
=C. A final editor checks consistency across slides and notes#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
~D. Let everyone edit without roles or version control#This choice weakens the communication product because it ignores how the audience will use or understand it.
}
